---
title: ytif · records from execution to board
config:
  look: classic
  theme: dark
  themeVariables:
    actorBkg: "#333333"
    labelBoxBkgColor: "#fcd34d"
    labelTextColor: "#000000"
    noteTextColor: "#e0e0e0"
  themeCSS: |
    /* collections · file */
    rect.actor:not([rx]) { fill: #3d3415; stroke: #fcd34d; }
  sequence:
    actorMargin: 80
    width: 200
    wrap: true
---
%% Behavior authority: internal/gate/gate.go (recordLines, writeRecords), internal/record/record.go, internal/cli/cli.go (runBoard), internal/board/board.go (Render), .github/workflows/ci.yml and README.md (Board).
%% CI upload is configured by the host workflow; ytif itself writes a local file. Artifact retention is also host-owned.
%% The record append occurs at gate finalization, including ordinary failures. An early exit or forced termination may leave no records; interrupted work has no completed result.
%% The board reads explicit --records paths or the default local file, never an implicit union or a remembered download.
sequenceDiagram
  participant CI as CI workflow<br/>runs ytif
  participant CIFile@{ "type": "collections", "alias": "Runner-local records" }
  participant Artifacts as GitHub Actions<br/>artifacts
  actor User as Developer
  participant Local as Local ytif<br/>gates and board
  participant Files@{ "type": "collections", "alias": "Local repository and files" }

  CI->>CI: Run ytif ci in the host-selected mode
  CI->>CIFile: Gate finalization: append one JSONL batch
  Note over CI,CIFile: • Results, timings and selection<br/>• Full output stays in the CI console
  opt Host workflow reaches its upload step
    CI->>CIFile: Read the configured record file, if present
    CIFile-->>CI: JSONL
    CI->>Artifacts: Upload ytif-records, also after a failed gate
  end

  opt Local gate execution
    User->>Local: Run check, commit, push or ci locally
    Local->>Files: At finalization, append default common-dir records
    Note over Local,Files: • Worktrees share local records<br/>• --records overrides the destination
  end

  opt Developer retrieves CI records
    User->>Artifacts: Select a workflow run and download its artifact
    Artifacts-->>User: Record file
    User->>Files: Save the downloaded JSONL
  end

  User->>Local: Run ytif board
  alt Explicit --records paths
    Local->>Files: Read only the specified local JSONL files
  else No --records flag
    Local->>Files: Read common-dir/ytif/records.jsonl
  end
  Files-->>Local: Outcomes, timing and available selection metadata
  Local->>Files: Read the current verification registry and includes
  Files-->>Local: Current membership, contracts and relations
  Local->>Local: Join by verification key and aggregate history
  Local->>Files: Write a static board.html snapshot
  Local-->>User: Open the page by default<br/>--out writes only
  Note over Local,Files: • HTML is a static snapshot<br/>• No remote fetch<br/>• No affected/full diagnosis
